# Task 155-003 Execution Plan: Model Registry Remote Refresh

## Files to Create/Modify
1. src/core/model-registry.ts — Add lastRefresh state + isStale() + setLastRefresh() + getLastRefresh()
2. src/core/model-registry-refresh.ts (NEW) — Refresh logic, state I/O, API calls, formatRefreshAge
3. src/cli/commands/doctor-checks.ts — Add checkModelRegistryStale() + runDoctorChecks integration
4. tests/core/model-registry-refresh.test.ts (NEW) — 8+ tests

## Design Decisions
- lastRefresh stored as in-memory Partial<Record<RegistryProviderName, number>> in ModelRegistry
- Persistence: .deckent/model-registry-refresh.json (timestamps only, not model defs)
- API calls: global fetch (Node 18+ built-in)
- No API key = graceful skip with hint (never throw)
- Malformed response = no crash (try/catch wraps all parsing)
- refreshAllProviders = Promise.all (parallel)
- doctor.ts --refresh-models: export runModelRegistryRefresh from doctor-checks.ts; 
  note: doctor.ts option wiring is outside filesWrite scope — exports are ready for wiring

## Test Matrix (8 tests)
1. loadRefreshState handles missing file → returns zero state
2. saveRefreshState + loadRefreshState round-trip
3. ModelRegistry.isStale() with no lastRefresh → true
4. ModelRegistry.isStale() with recent timestamp → false  
5. ModelRegistry.isStale() after staleAfterMs → true
6. refreshProvider no api key → success=false + skippedReason (graceful)
7. refreshProvider malformed API response → no crash, success=false
8. refreshAllProviders parallel → all 3 providers resolved
